SOLUTION
==========================================
What does the program until now 
==========================================
Falco: It monitors the system activities and detects behaviors that match the security rules that we defined. 
       It is configured using the modern eBPF engine and generates events in JSON format.

Policies (policy.py): It receives the events and determines the action based on configured rules.
The main categories for response are ignore,alerts, or isolates a container.

Isolation (isolation_recovery_container.py): Takes actions on containers using the Docker SDK. 
It allows  disconnecting their networks, pausing their execution, or even stopping, as well as their recovery.

Notification Module (notification_alerter.py): Logs incidents into JSONL files and enables the sending 
of notifications to external services via Webhooks.

Main API (Main_alert_falco.py): Developed using FastAPI, it receives events sent by Falco, 
performs token-based authentication, and coordinates the policy engine, container isolation, and notifications.

===========================================
FILES
===========================================
File                            ||  Function 
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
policy.py	->                  Evaluates events and determines whether to ignore them, generate alerts, or isolate containers.
isolation_recovery_container.py ->  Perform isolation and recovery of Docker containers.
notification_alerter.py	    -> Manage alerts, logs, and external notifications.
Main_alert_falco.py	           -> Main API that connects Falco with the Sentinel_Falco modules.
policy_rules_defined.yaml	    -> Define policies, exceptions, and response actions.
rules_detection_falco.yaml	    -> Contains custom rules for detecting threats.
configfalco.yaml	          ->  Specific configuration for Falco to integrate it with Sentinel_Falco.
falco-guard.env                ->  Authentication and operating mode configuration file.


============================================
RULES
============================================
The events that triggers the rules are the following 
Unauthorized access to the host file system.

Modification of files related to container escapes.
Access to Docker sockets and other runtime services.
Execution of `nsenter` commands within containers.
Detection of system calls related to mount operations.
Identification of interactive shell sessions.

NOTE: A scaling mechanism based on the number of events detected within a time interval is also included.

===============================================
ISOLATION
==============================================

Pause its execution to prevent it from continuing to carry out suspicious activities.
Stop the container.
Preserve the information before applying isolation (Gathers data about the container)
Subsequently recover the container, restoring its execution state and network connections based on the actions taken.

==============================================
REGISTER/LOGS
=============================================
Before the isolation happens, the system collects information such as its configuration attributes, file system differences,
active processes, and recent logs. Sensitive variables are partially masked to avoid the direct storage of passwords or tokens.

==============================================
OPTIONS OF FUNCTIONING 
==============================================
DETECTION_MODE: simulation mode. just to detect and alert
ENFORCE: it includes isolation


